{"task_id": "Mbpp/86", "solution": "def centered_hexagonal_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth centered hexagonal number using the formula C(n) = 3*n*(n-1)+1.\n    Assumes n is a positive integer (n >= 1).\n    \"\"\"\n    return 3 * n * (n - 1) + 1"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "def sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence using dynamic programming.\n    Results are memoized on the function object to optimize repeated calculations.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not hasattr(sequence, \"_cache\"):\n        sequence._cache = {1: 1, 2: 1}\n\n    if n in sequence._cache:\n        return sequence._cache[n]\n\n    # Initialize a temporary array for dynamic programming up to n.\n    # We populate it with known cached values and base cases.\n    dp_array = [0] * (n + 1)\n\n    # Fill base cases and existing cached values into dp_array.\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        if i in sequence._cache:\n            dp_array[i] = sequence._cache[i]\n        elif i <= 2: # Base cases for the Newman-Conway sequence\n            dp_array[i] = 1\n            sequence._cache[i] = 1\n\n    # Compute missing values from 3 up to n using the sequence definition.\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        if dp_array[i] == 0:  # Only compute if not already in cache\n            prev_val = dp_array[i - 1]\n            dp_array[i] = dp_array[prev_val] + dp_array[i - prev_val]\n            sequence._cache[i] = dp_array[i]\n\n    return dp_array[n]"}
