{"task_id": "Mbpp/172", "solution": "def count_occurance(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of occurrences of the substring 'std' in the given string.\n    Overlapping occurrences are counted.\n    \"\"\"\n    pattern = \"std\"\n    n = len(s)\n    m = len(pattern)\n    \n    if m == 0 or n < m:\n        return 0\n        \n    count = 0\n    for i in range(n - m + 1):\n        if s[i : i + m] == pattern:\n            count += 1\n            \n    return count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def is_majority(arr, n, x):\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if an element x is the majority element in a sorted array arr of length n.\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _first_occurrence(array, target):\n        \"\"\"\n        Finds the first occurrence of target in a sorted array using binary search.\n        Returns the index of the first occurrence or -1 if not found.\n        \"\"\"\n        lo, hi = 0, len(array) - 1\n        res = -1\n        while lo <= hi:\n            mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n            if array[mid] == target:\n                res = mid\n                hi = mid - 1\n            elif array[mid] < target:\n                lo = mid + 1\n            else:\n                hi = mid - 1\n        return res\n\n    first_idx = _first_occurrence(arr, x)\n\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return False\n\n    # The majority element must occur more than n/2 times.\n    # If the element at first_idx + n//2 is also x, it means x occurs at least n//2 + 1 times.\n    check_idx = first_idx + n // 2\n\n    return check_idx < n and arr[check_idx] == x"}
