{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets all even bits (1-indexed positions 2, 4, 6, ... which are 0-indexed positions 1, 3, 5, ...)\n    of the given non-negative integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Determine the effective bit length for the mask, ensuring it's at least 1 for n=0.\n    bit_length = max(1, n.bit_length())\n\n    # Construct a mask with bits set at 0-indexed odd positions (1, 3, 5, ...)\n    mask = 0\n    for i in range(bit_length):\n        if i % 2 == 1:  # Check if the 0-indexed bit position is odd\n            mask |= (1 << i)\n\n    # Perform a bitwise OR operation to set the specified bits in n.\n    return n | mask"}
