{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "from typing import Optional\n\ndef set_left_most_unset_bit(value: int, width: Optional[int] = None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets the left-most unset bit in the given non-negative integer.\n\n    The search scope is determined by 'width' or the value's bit length.\n    \"\"\"\n    if width is not None:\n        # Search from width-1 down to 0\n        for pos in range(width - 1, -1, -1):\n            if not ((value >> pos) & 1):  # If bit at 'pos' is 0\n                return value | (1 << pos)\n        # If all bits within the specified width are set, set the bit at position 'width'\n        return value | (1 << width)\n    else:\n        # Determine the effective bit length, ensuring at least 1 for value=0\n        bl = max(1, value.bit_length())\n        \n        # Search from bl-1 down to 0\n        for pos in range(bl - 1, -1, -1):\n            if not ((value >> pos) & 1):  # If bit at 'pos' is 0\n                return value | (1 << pos)\n        # If all bits up to bl-1 are set, set the bit at position 'bl'\n        return value | (1 << bl)"}
